{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793373949,"nonce":"ApPXZfmB9alFmHUvr6bVqJ3nVaM=","message":"Phase A and the desktop half of phase B started: native/sync (crate rayde-sync, a17f803), 61 tests passing (45 contract and policy tests, 16 against real Git repositories). The pure modules build for wasm32 without the `scan` feature, so the Worker can validate exactly what the desktop produced.\n\nDecisions the contracts make (change them here first):\n- Workspace id: 32 random bytes as 43 base64url characters (the form the gateway's `/{id}` routes already accept), canonical in the last symbol so two ids cannot name one workspace. Not derived from owner, repository or path. Account id: the account directory's id, never an OAuth session, email or GitHub login.\n- Roles and operations: Owner \u003e Editor \u003e Viewer. Viewer: read only. Editor: files, documents, Git mutation and export. Owner alone: share, expiry, allocation, delete, transfer. Run, Terminal and Extensions need the owner or an explicit per-kind grant to an editor; a viewer never holds one. A link is Viewer or Editor, needs the current rotation and a signed-in account, and carries no grants; the higher of a membership and a link applies. Anonymous is denied everywhere.\n- Revocation: every change that reduces access (remove member, lower role, take a grant, change or rotate or disable the link) advances `acl_version`; a Lease (publish or execution) records the version it was issued under and the generation it saw, and stops holding when either moved or the clock passed. Invitations are scoped to one role, expire, are revocable, bound to an account when they name one.\n- Expiry: server time; the clock starts at the first successful publication only; viewing, compute restarts and retries never extend it; shortening never lengthens; renewal is the owner's explicit act within the plan; every change advances `version` so a cleanup job queued under an older version cannot delete a renewed workspace. Retained storage needs the entitlement and has no deadline. Default 24 hours, default allocation 1 GB (1,000,000,000 bytes), free pilot plan: 3 workspaces, 3 GB total (placeholder numbers, to be replaced by the entitlement catalog; the 1, 10, 50 and 100 GB retained sizes stay proposals).\n- Quota: a reservation counts bytes in flight as well as referenced bytes, against both the workspace allocation (capped by the plan) and the account total, so two uploads that each fit cannot together exceed the budget; refusal never charges; an abandoned upload returns its reservation.\n- Limits checked before upload (defaults for the pilot): 100,000 files, 100 MB per file, expanded size = allocation, history = half the allocation, 256 buffers of at most 8 MiB, paths at most 1024 bytes and 64 deep.\n- Manifest (format 1): files as ordered chunk references (SHA-256, content-defined chunks of 256 KiB to 4 MiB averaging about 1 MiB, so an edited large file uploads only what changed), symlinks as relative targets never dereferenced, executable bit only, tracked or untracked origin; Git state as branch, head, unborn flag, index entries (staged versus unstaged without copying .git), deleted tracked paths, submodule paths (listed, not dereferenced), LFS flag, and the history as a Git bundle of branches, tags and HEAD (a bundle carries objects and refs and no hooks, config or credentials; verified); unsaved editor buffers kept apart from saved files with the hash of their base; omissions with reasons; totals; a checksum over the canonical form. A golden fixture (native/sync/tests/fixtures/manifest-v1.json) must read and verify in every client and the gateway.\n- Exclusions: `.git` (any case, any depth) and RayDE session state never leave and cannot be chosen; credentials (env files except templates, keys, certificates, netrc, cloud and SSH directories, tfstate) need an explicit decision even when tracked; caches and ambiguous output directories (bin, dist, build, out, target, export) are left out only when Git does not track them; OS litter is left out; a cache directory is one omission, not thousands.\n\nNot done, by design here: no network, no Worker routes, no sidebar. Next: the gateway's sync API (reserve, upload chunks, publish with compare and swap) and the desktop client that uploads a snapshot; both are filed as separate issues below. Both depend on the account and PKCE sign-in work (92e2f4e), which also does not exist yet; fixtures and the local R2 emulation can proceed first, as in the plan.","files":null}]}